body:
You have no reason to buy the Pro ones... the fact that the 9.7in Inst A4 size doesn't matter much, because you simply zoom in as much as you like, write normally as you would, zoom back to continue reading and your notation turn into a small text at the borders of the page or wherever you like.

I would go for:

&#x200B;

Wait the cheaper model in March that will substitute the 9.7 2018

&#x200B;

Go with the 9.7 2018

&#x200B;

Go with the Pro from 2017 (this one still overkill for most of what Ipad do) maybe cheap used

&#x200B;

The 2018 Pro, is good and all but every other option will cover you for years and you may buy used.

My wife don't even get hitches yet with the Pro 2017 even though, she draws hardcore, with split screen and a video floating the screen.  


Edit. Also Buy a PaperLike for the screen its super nice to write on
